course: dictionary
lesson: 3254
title: Episcopal: churches led by bishops
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Churches are run in different ways. Episcopal means led by bishops. A bishop is a senior church leader who looks after many churches in an area.
explain: «The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA; episcopal means led by bishops.» The name tells you how the church is run, so you can work out its type from its name.
explain: In RE, churches are sorted by how they are led. Episcopal churches are led by bishops, presbyterian churches are led by elders, and congregational churches let each congregation decide for itself.
explain: Some names use a capital E, such as the Episcopal Church and the Scottish Episcopal Church. These are the names of particular Anglican churches, so they are not just the same as the general word.
fact: Episcopal means about bishops, or led by bishops.
fact: The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA.
fact: The Scottish Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in Scotland.
fact: In the USA and Scotland, an Anglican is often called an Episcopalian.
fact: Presbyterian churches are led by elders, and congregational churches are run by each congregation.
exercise: «The Episcopal Church is the Anglican church in the USA.» What does episcopal mean? | Led by children | Led by elders | *Led by bishops | Each congregation decides
exercise: Which word means a church led by elders? | Anglican | Episcopal | *Presbyterian | Congregational
exercise: Which of these churches is episcopal? | Congregational | Baptist | *Catholic | Presbyterian
test: Which church is the Anglican church in Scotland? | Methodist Church | *Scottish Episcopal Church | Baptist Church | Presbyterian Church
test: What does congregational mean? | *Each congregation decides for itself | Led by elders | The Pope decides everything | Led by bishops
exam: Which meaning fits episcopal? | *Led by bishops | Led by elders | A very old building | Having no leaders at all
